<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Q4 private wages rise 0.8 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Q4 private wages rise 0.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private sector average weekly ordinary time earnings (AWOTE) rose 0.8 percent in the three months to November for a rise of 2.8 percent on the year, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Public sector AWOTE rose 2.2 percent in the quarter to be up 7.6 percent over the previous 12 months.</p>
<p>Final AWOTE data for adults employed full time was unrevised from the preliminary estimates, showing a 1.2 percent quarterly rise for annual AWOTE growth of 3.9 percent.  </p>
<p>Average weekly ordinary adult earnings (percentage change):</p>
<p>					  Aug 96-Nov 96  Nov 95 - Nov 96</p>
<p>     Seasonally adjusted	    +1.2		  +3.9</p>
<p>     Trend				+1.1		  +4.1</p>
<p>     Unadjusted			 +1.3		  +3.9</p>
<p>Private sector AWOTE</p>
<p>     Seasonally adjusted	    +0.8		  +2.8</p>
<p>     Trend				+0.8		  +3.1</p>
<p>     Unadjusted			 +0.9		  +2.8</p>
<p>Public sector AWOTE</p>
<p>     Seasonally adjusted	    +2.2		  +7.6</p>
<p>     Trend				+2.2		  +7.3</p>
<p>     Unadjusted			 +2.7		  +7.6</p>
</text>
